# Dashboard UI

Kame Finance is **dashboard-first** (no large public marketing surface in v1). Guest-facing or embeddable UIs may come later for specific modules.

## Layout

- Use `(dashboard)` route group with sidebar + header
- Semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border` (see `apps/web/DESIGN.md`)
- Support light and dark mode on every new screen

## Module Pages

| Nav | Route | Primary UX |
| --- | ----- | ---------- |
| Home | `/dashboard` | Month header (‹ NOVEMBER 2026 ›, Month/Year), month calendar with due/statement marks, "Needs you" list, month summary ledger, spend by category, first-run checklist |
| Bills | `/dashboard/bills` | Open month's bills (due entries + receipts per card): filters, mark paid/unpaid, upload receipt, view payment; `?view=receipts` receipt board; `#bill-<id>` deep link |
| Statements | `/dashboard/statements` | Statement months by year → month detail (Summary / Cards / Transactions / Analytics) → statement detail |
| Cards | `/dashboard/cards` | Card rows; add/edit in a sectioned side sheet (`?add=1`, `?edit=<id>`) |
| Settings | `/dashboard/settings?section=` | Connections, Automations (payment reminders, SOA Gmail check), Statements, Categories, AI |

Legacy paths (`/dashboard/soa`, `/credit-cards`, `/reminders`, `/receipts`, `/automations`) redirect via `LEGACY_DASHBOARD_REDIRECTS` in `config/routes.ts`.

## Data Tables

Use TanStack Table v8 via shared `DataTable` patterns. Credit card and reminder lists should support sort, filter, and row actions.

## Actions & Destructive Flows

- Confirm before deleting cards or disconnecting integrations
- SOA run: show progress states (searching Gmail, parsing, notifying)
- Mark paid: optimistic UI optional; always show server error messages

## Empty States

- One short title + optional single line + CTA — no essays unless user requests copy
- Link to settings only when the action truly requires configuration elsewhere

## Do Not

- Add unsolicited descriptions, helper paragraphs, or `CardDescription` prose (see `21-minimal-ui-copy.mdc`)
- Put SOA parsing logic in components—call tRPC mutations that invoke services
- Hardcode bank list in UI—load from server constants or DB
